🔐 HMAC vs JWT vs OAuth
1️⃣ HMAC (Low-level security mechanism)

👉 What it is:
A cryptographic technique to sign data using a secret key

👉 Purpose:

Ensure data integrity + authenticity

👉 Used in:

API request signing
Webhooks
Inside JWT (sometimes)

👉 Key point:

Uses shared secret key

👉 Example flow:

HMAC = H(secret + message)
2️⃣ JWT (JSON Web Token)

👉 What it is:
A token format used for authentication

👉 Structure:

Header.Payload.Signature

👉 Purpose:

Stateless authentication
Carry user data (claims)

👉 Uses HMAC internally

Example: HS256 = HMAC + SHA-256

👉 Example:

eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOjEyM30.signature

👉 Key point:

Can be signed using:
HMAC (shared key)
RSA (public/private key)
3️⃣ OAuth (Authorization Framework)

👉 What it is:
A protocol that allows apps to access user data without sharing passwords

👉 Purpose:

Authorization (not authentication directly)

👉 Example:

“Login with Google”
“Login with Facebook”

👉 Flow (simplified):

User logs in via Google
Google gives access token
Your app uses token to access user data

👉 Key point:

Uses tokens (often JWT) internally
🧠 Simple Comparison Table
| Feature   | HMAC          | JWT                      | OAuth         |
| --------- | ------------- | ------------------------ | ------------- |
| Type      | Algorithm     | Token format             | Protocol      |
| Purpose   | Sign data     | Authentication           | Authorization |
| Uses key  | Shared secret | Secret or public/private | Uses tokens   |
| Stateless | ❌             | ✅                        | ✅             |
| Real use  | API security  | Login sessions           | Social login  |

🔗 Relationship (Important for interview)

👉 Very important concept:

OAuth → gives token
JWT → is the token format
HMAC → signs the token

💡 One line:

OAuth uses JWT tokens, and JWT can be signed using HMAC.

☕ Java Example (HMAC - Very Important)

Using built-in Java:

import javax.crypto.Mac;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import java.util.Base64;

public class HmacExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        String secret = "mySecretKey";
        String message = "HelloWorld";

        Mac mac = Mac.getInstance("HmacSHA256");
        SecretKeySpec keySpec = new SecretKeySpec(secret.getBytes(), "HmacSHA256");
        mac.init(keySpec);

        byte[] hmacBytes = mac.doFinal(message.getBytes());
        String hmac = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(hmacBytes);

        System.out.println("HMAC: " + hmac);
    }
}
